# BrogueMCP Cursor Rules System

This document provides a comprehensive guide to the BrogueMCP Cursor rules system - a sophisticated framework for maintaining code quality, consistency, and development standards across the project. This system is designed to make roguelike development more efficient by providing context-aware guidance and automated rule enforcement.

## Core Capabilities

The BrogueMCP Cursor rules system provides the following capabilities:

- **Coding Standards**: Automated enforcement of C coding standards specific to roguelike development
- **Procedural Generation Patterns**: Guidelines for implementing efficient procedural content generation
- **Memory Management**: Patterns for efficient memory usage in procedural environments
- **Cross-Platform Support**: Guidelines for maintaining compatibility across operating systems
- **AI Integration**: Framework for integrating the Dungeon Master agent
- **Self-Healing Rules**: Automatic detection and resolution of common errors

## Rule Structure

Each rule file follows a consistent structure:

```markdown
---
title: "Rule Title"
description: "Brief description of the rule"
glob: "pattern/to/match/**"
priority: 500
related: ["related-rule-1.mdc", "related-rule-2.mdc"]
---

# Rule Title

## Overview
Brief overview of what the rule covers

## Guidelines
Specific guidance for implementation

## Examples
Code examples demonstrating proper usage
```

